<title>USA: Minn. Development repriced, yields raised.</title>
<headline>Minn. Development repriced, yields raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Smith Barney Inc. said Wednesday it repriced Minnesota Agricultural and Economic Development Board $175 million bond deal, raising yields in several maturities and the top yield to 6.04 percent from 6.02.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:</p>
<p>MINNESOTA AGRICULTURAL AND ECONOMIC DEVELOPMENT</p>
<p>BOARD, HEALTH CARE SYSTEM REVENUE BONDS,SERIES 97A</p>
<p>RE: $174,935,000*</p>
<p>(FAIRVIEW HOSPITAL AND HEALTHCARE SERVICES)</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>PLEASE NOTE THE REPRICING 1999, 2000, 2017 AND 2026.</p>
<p>THE FOLLOWING MATURITIES ARE OVERSUBSCRIBED: 2001 THROUGH 2003, 2008, 2011 AND</p>
